{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Behold, I have given into your hand Sihon</b> — this utterance is what is said below (Deuteronomy 2:31): 'Behold, I have begun to give before you,' and before that, he sent messengers to him from the wilderness of Kedemoth. For after HaShem commanded him, 'Begin, take possession, and contend with him in battle,' he would not send him words of peace, 'Let me pass through your land,' for if he listened to him, he would be transgressing the word of HaShem, and if he knew that he would not listen, his mission would be in vain. And do not think to say that this is the commandment regarding which we were commanded (Deuteronomy 20:10): 'When you draw near to a city to fight against it, you shall call out to it for peace' — for there it is written (Deuteronomy 20:11): 'And it shall be that all the people found in it shall become tribute to you and serve you,' whereas here, if he had listened to them, they would not have touched him at all. But the meaning of <b>and I sent messengers</b> is: I have already sent messengers. But he prefaced with the word of HaShem to explain that 'HaShem your Elohim hardened his spirit' (Deuteronomy 2:30) — to say that everything was a cause from HaShem, for thus He said to me:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Ramban cites Deuteronomy 20:11 but the verse number in his text reads ב':י\"א (2:11); he clearly intends chapter 20, v. 11, as the content quoted matches that verse exactly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:44:29.708520786Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}